      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_timeout.result"><source>The source was read. No results were created, and nothing was published.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_timeout.action"><source>Wait a few minutes. Start the job again with the button below.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_timeout.admin"><source>If it keeps failing, ask your administrator to look at the AI provider: its status and the timeout in the AI configuration.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_rate_limited.short"><source>The AI service refused for now: too many requests</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_rate_limited.what"><source>The AI service limits how many requests it takes at a time, and this job went over that limit.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_rate_limited.result"><source>The source was read. No results were created, and nothing was published.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_rate_limited.action"><source>Wait a while. Start the job again with the button below.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_rate_limited.admin"><source>If it keeps failing, ask your administrator to check the rate limit of the provider account.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_unavailable.short"><source>The AI service is not available</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_unavailable.what"><source>The AI service answered with an error. This job cannot do anything about that.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_unavailable.result"><source>The source was read. No results were created, and nothing was published.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_unavailable.action"><source>Wait a while. Start the job again with the button below.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_unavailable.admin"><source>If it keeps failing, ask your administrator to look at the AI provider under AI &gt; Overview.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_setup.short"><source>The AI service is not set up correctly</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_setup.what"><source>The AI service could not be used with the configured access: a key, a configuration or a permission is missing or wrong.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_setup.result"><source>The source was read. No results were created, and nothing was published.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_setup.action"><source>You cannot solve this yourself. Once your administrator has corrected it, start the job again with the button below.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.provider_setup.admin"><source>Ask your administrator to check the AI provider, its API key and the AI configuration "Content Repurpose: Text".</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.budget_exhausted.short"><source>The AI budget is used up</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.budget_exhausted.what"><source>The AI budget of the user who created this job is used up, so the AI service was not called any more.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.budget_exhausted.result"><source>No results were created, and nothing was published.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.budget_exhausted.action"><source>Wait until the budget renews, or ask for more. Then start the job again with the button below.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.budget_exhausted.admin"><source>Your administrator sets the budget under AI &gt; Operation &gt; Analysis and in the user budgets.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.budget_or_service.short"><source>AI budget used up, or the service is not available</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.budget_or_service.what"><source>The image or speech service could not be used. Either the AI budget is used up, or the service is not available.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.budget_or_service.result"><source>Only this format is affected. Other formats of the job are not.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.budget_or_service.action"><source>Create a new job with only this format once the budget renews or the service is back.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.budget_or_service.admin"><source>Ask your administrator whether a budget is used up, and whether an AI configuration for images and speech is set up.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.guardrail.short"><source>A content rule stopped this</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.guardrail.what"><source>A content rule of this installation refused the text. The reason is named below.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.guardrail.result"><source>No results were created, and nothing was published.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.guardrail.action"><source>Change the source so that it meets the rule, and create a new job.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.guardrail.admin"><source>If you think the rule is wrong for this text, ask your administrator. The rules are set in the AI configuration.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.not_permitted.short"><source>Your user group may not create this format</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.not_permitted.what"><source>Podcast audio and AI images need a permission that the backend groups of the job's creator do not grant.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.not_permitted.result"><source>Only this format is affected. Other formats of the job are not.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.not_permitted.action"><source>Create a new job without this format, or ask for the permission.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.not_permitted.admin"><source>Your administrator grants it in the backend group, under custom options: "Generate podcast audio" and "Generate AI imagery".</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.rendering.short"><source>The file for this format could not be made</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.rendering.what"><source>The text is there, but the program on the server that makes the image, PDF, audio or video file failed.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.rendering.result"><source>Only this format is affected. Other formats of the job are not.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.rendering.action"><source>You cannot solve this yourself. Create a new job for this format once your administrator has looked at it.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.rendering.admin"><source>Ask your administrator to check Chromium and ffmpeg on the worker.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.some_formats_failed.short"><source>Some formats failed</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.some_formats_failed.what"><source>Some formats are finished, others failed. Each failed format says why further down.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.some_formats_failed.result"><source>The finished formats are complete and can be used.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.some_formats_failed.action"><source>To make the failed formats, create a new job with only those formats. Starting this job again would remove the finished ones.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.some_formats_failed.admin"><source>Each failed format says whether it needs your administrator.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.all_formats_failed.short"><source>All formats failed</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.all_formats_failed.what"><source>The source was read and analysed, but no format could be made. Each format says why further down.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.all_formats_failed.result"><source>No finished results exist, and nothing was published.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.all_formats_failed.action"><source>Read the reasons further down. Start the job again with the button below.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.all_formats_failed.admin"><source>Each format says whether it needs your administrator.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.internal.short"><source>An internal error stopped the job</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.internal.what"><source>Something went wrong in the extension or on the server. Your source and your settings are not the cause.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.internal.result"><source>No results were created, and nothing was published.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.internal.action"><source>Start the job again with the button below. If it happens again, ask your administrator.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.internal.admin"><source>This needs your administrator if it happens again.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.worker_stalled.short"><source>No progress for more than two hours</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.worker_stalled.what"><source>This job has not moved for more than two hours. The background service that processes jobs is probably not running.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.worker_stalled.result"><source>Nothing was lost. The job continues by itself once the service runs again.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.worker_stalled.action"><source>You cannot solve this yourself. You do not need to create the job again.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.worker_stalled.admin"><source>Ask your administrator to check the Messenger worker of this installation.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.unknown.short"><source>The job failed, the reason was not saved</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.unknown.what"><source>This job failed with an older version of the extension, which did not save the reason for this page.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.unknown.result"><source>Nothing was published.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.unknown.action"><source>Start the job again with the button below. If it fails again, this page names the reason.</source></trans-unit>
      <trans-unit id="failure.unknown.admin"><source>Your administrator can read the error in the log.</source></trans-unit>

